<title>UK: Orange up after positive comment from Capel.</title>
<headline>Orange up after positive comment from Capel.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in mobile telephone company Orange Group rose on Tuesday, helped by recent positive comment from analysts at HSBC James Capel, dealers said.</p>
<p>By 1343 GMT, shares in Orange were 1-1/2p higher at 195 on volume of 3.4 million.</p>
<p>Capel analyst Martin Mabbut said he had re-iterated his positive stance on the stock on Monday.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
